Hello,
I created a custom flight task sending attitude setpoints (bypassing the position control).
After exiting the flight task, switch to POSITION Mode. The attitude setpoint is given by the position control (here the existing code in Position control)
// Publish attitude setpoint output
			vehicle_attitude_setpoint_s attitude_setpoint{};
			_control.getAttitudeSetpoint(attitude_setpoint);
			attitude_setpoint.timestamp = hrt_absolute_time();
			_vehicle_attitude_setpoint_pub.publish(attitude_setpoint);
But there is no attitude set point in the logs.
When checking in both Position control and attitude control, seems that the position setpoints are not valid
_vehicle_attitude_setpoint_sub.updated()
gives false. But it gives true if the flight task is never enabled during the flight.
Any idea?

